1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,440
Okay, moving on to bone tumors.

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:03,580
The first tumor is an osteoma.

3
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,340
Osteo means bone, and oma means mass.

4
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,360
So this is a benign tumor of bone.

5
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:11,360
Now there are two high yields for an osteoma.

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,740
Number one, it most commonly arises

7
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:16,120
on the surface of facial bones.

8
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,580
And number two, it's associated with Gardner syndrome.

9
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,640
Now recall from our GI lecture

10
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:25,460
that Gardner syndrome is familial adenomatous polyposis

11
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:29,040
plus fibromatosis in the retroperitinium,

12
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:32,020
and again, fibromatosis is a non-neoplastic

13
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:34,620
proliferation of fibroblasts that grows

14
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:36,260
and locally destroys tissue.

15
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,880
And then number three, osteomas of the facial bone.

16
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,440
And so here we're talking about those osteomas

17
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,300
that are associated with Gardner syndrome.

18
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:47,500
So that's particularly high yield for board examinations.

19
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:52,740
Osteoid osteoma is a benign tumor of osteoblasts.

20
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,600
Remember that osteoblasts are the cells that lay down bone,

21
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:56,860
but they don't make bone.

22
00:00:56,940 --> 00:00:58,360
They make something called osteoid.

23
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,260
And osteoid is a matrix that gets mineralized,

24
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,580
and when it gets mineralized with calcium and phosphate,

25
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,060
then it becomes bone.

26
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,560
And so this tumor produces osteoid,

27
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,040
and in response to this osteoid,

28
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,920
so imagine this is the osteoid here,

29
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:18,120
you get a rim of sclerotic sort of reactive bone,

30
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,620
and that's what's called the osteoma.

31
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:23,520
So basically here is the osteoid,

32
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,060
and here this rim is the osteoma.

33
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:28,780
So let's read this now.

34
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,320
So this is a benign tumor of osteoblasts,

35
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,340
which make osteoid,

36
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,840
surrounded by a rim of reactive bone,

37
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,360
hence the term osteoma.

38
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,160
It occurs in the cortex of young adults,

39
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:40,780
less than 25 years of age,

40
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,320
which is sort of the classic demographic,

41
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,420
and it arises in the cortex of long bones.

42
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,040
Now let's go back and remind ourselves

43
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,200
that the bone has a cortex,

44
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,260
which is its surface,

45
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:50,840
and then there's a medulla.

46
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:52,860
And so this tumor is going to arise

47
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:54,660
on the cortex of the bone,

48
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,200
and also important to note

49
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,460
is that it usually arises

50
00:01:57,460 --> 00:02:00,780
on the diaphysis in a long bone.

51
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:02,020
So for example,

52
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,580
if this is the growth plate,

53
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:05,120
then above the growth plate

54
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:05,780
is called the epiphysis.

55
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:07,700
The growth plate region

56
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:08,820
is called the metaphysis,

57
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:10,680
and this long shaft here

58
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,800
is called the diaphysis.

59
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,880
And so osteoid osteoma

60
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,320
usually occurs on the cortex

61
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,680
of a long bone

62
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:18,840
in the region of the diaphysis.

63
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,380
Now the presentation is also important,

64
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,700
and that is that the patients have bone pain,

65
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,160
but it resolves with aspirin.

66
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:27,800
And examiners really like you to know

67
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,740
that in an osteoid osteoma,

68
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,540
the bone pain resolves with aspirin.

69
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:33,240
Now when imaging is performed,

70
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,480
you'll see a bony mass

71
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,100
with a radiolucent core.

72
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:37,280
Again, the idea here

73
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:37,800
is that you've got

74
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,680
a center core of osteoid,

75
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,340
which will be radiolucent.

76
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,980
It won't get picked up on the x-ray.

77
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:45,620
However, that will be surrounded

78
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:48,100
by a rim of reactive bone,

79
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,220
which will light up as white on the x-ray,

80
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:52,660
i.e. the color of bone.

81
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:54,280
And so that's what we mean here

82
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,940
when we say that you get a bony mass

83
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:58,120
with a radiolucent core.

84
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:00,040
The bony mass represents the rim,

85
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,900
and the center, the core,

86
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:03,340
represents the osteoid.

87
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:06,740
Now osteoblastoma is a benign tumor of osteoblast.

88
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,300
It's very similar to osteoid osteoma

89
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:12,020
because that was also a benign tumor of osteoblast.

90
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:14,740
However, there are three key differences

91
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:15,960
that are very high yield.

92
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,360
Osteoblastoma is larger.

93
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,380
An osteoid osteoma is usually less than two centimeters,

94
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:24,480
and osteoblastoma is usually greater than two centimeters.

95
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:27,920
The osteoblastoma usually arises in the vertebra.

96
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:32,640
Remember that the osteoid osteoma arose on the cortex

97
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,940
of the diaphysis of long bones.

98
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:39,320
And number three, an osteoblastoma presents as bone pain

99
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,300
that does not respond to aspirin, very high yield.

100
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,420
Whereas with an osteoid osteoma,

101
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,400
the bone pain would respond to aspirin.

102
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,880
Osteochondroma is a benign tumor of bone

103
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,340
with an overlying cartilage cap.

104
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:55,580
It's the most common benign tumor of bone,

105
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:59,080
and it arises from a lateral projection of the growth plate.

106
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:00,640
Now let's illustrate this.

107
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:02,420
Here is the bone.

108
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,640
This is the growth plate.

109
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,640
And recall that the growth plate is made of cartilage.

110
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:10,080
Now as the growth plate expands,

111
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:14,860
it will then result in the elongation of the bone,

112
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,240
producing linear growth.

113
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:19,140
Now imagine if you had a lateral projection

114
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:20,680
of the growth plate like this,

115
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:24,080
then that would then subsequently result in,

116
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,020
for example, a projection of bone

117
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:28,880
with a surface of cartilage on it

118
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,900
that would look like this,

119
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,860
because this here would actually also grow,

120
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:34,140
but it would grow this way.

121
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:38,560
And so this then results in the tumor osteochondroma.

122
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,780
So again, if this was the tumor here,

123
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,400
the bone here represents the osteo,

124
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,380
and this cartilage cap that came

125
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,460
from that lateral projection of the growth plate

126
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,380
represents the chondro,

127
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,300
and the oma represents the mass,

128
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,640
so osteochondroma.

129
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,640
Here's a picture of an osteochondroma.

130
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:57,140
This entire thing represents the osteochondroma.

131
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,900
Imagine that it would be coming off

132
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,040
the surface of bone here.

133
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,560
So again, what would have happened

134
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,920
is you had a lateral projection

135
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,120
of the growth plate.

136
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,200
The lateral projection of the growth plate

137
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:07,940
will then grow,

138
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:09,300
and when it grows,

139
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:11,020
you'll get a surface of cartilage.

140
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:13,540
Notice this white here represents the cartilage,

141
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,660
underlying which would be bone,

142
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:16,900
and this represents bone.

143
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:18,500
And one of the important things

144
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:20,100
is that this will normally be contiguous

145
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,720
with the marrow space of the bone

146
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,540
from which it's growing.

147
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:24,360
So if this was the bone from which it's growing,

148
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:27,480
it'll attach and be contiguous

149
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,640
with the marrow space,

150
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,360
and that's also very important

151
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,100
considering an osteochondroma.

152
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:33,240
Now the final point

153
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,560
is that overlying cartilage

154
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:36,280
on the top of the osteochondroma

155
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:39,380
can transform into a malignant cartilage tumor,

156
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:41,920
and that would be called a chondrosarcoma,

157
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:44,180
and that's particularly important as well.

158
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:47,200
Osteosarcoma is a malignant tumor of bone.

159
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,540
Osteo means bone,

160
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,880
and sarcoma means malignant mesenchymal tumor.

161
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:51,880
And of course,

162
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,860
it's the osteoblasts that make bone,

163
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:55,780
and so the proliferation is actually

164
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,080
of the osteoblast.

165
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,640
Now the peak incidence is seen in teenagers,

166
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:00,980
but less commonly,

167
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:02,400
it can also be seen in the elderly.

168
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,520
Here's a graph of the peak incidence,

169
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:06,320
so here is the teenagers,

170
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,240
and here are the elderly.

171
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,240
Of course, this would be the incidence.

172
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:12,940
Now it's important to note

173
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,540
that some of the risk factors

174
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,000
that lead to osteosarcoma

175
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,880
include familial retinoblastoma.

176
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,480
Familial retinoblastoma,

177
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,220
recall from our neoplasia lectures,

178
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:22,580
leads to an increased risk

179
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:24,500
for biolateral retinoblastoma

180
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,660
and osteosarcoma,

181
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,960
particularly high yield.

182
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:29,480
And that would be something

183
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:32,020
that would lead to risk within teenagers.

184
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:33,260
In addition,

185
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,120
we have a peak here with the elderly,

186
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,720
and there are two very high yield risk factors

187
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,500
to be aware of.

188
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:41,320
Number one is Paget's disease of bone.

189
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:43,100
Recall that when we talked

190
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,520
about Paget's disease of bone,

191
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,400
I told you that it normally occurs

192
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,380
at the age of 60,

193
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:48,880
and I also told you

194
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:49,960
that one of the complications

195
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,720
was osteosarcoma.

196
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:52,580
And do you remember

197
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,520
the second complication?

198
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:55,940
The second complication was

199
00:06:55,940 --> 00:06:57,580
high output cardiac failure.

200
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:58,500
But anyway,

201
00:06:58,980 --> 00:06:59,880
Paget's disease of bone

202
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:00,720
has an increased risk

203
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,840
for osteosarcoma.

204
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,560
And the second important thing

205
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,840
that leads to an increased risk

206
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,380
in the elderly

207
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,620
would be radiation.

208
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,220
So radiation exposure

209
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,440
would increase the risk

210
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:10,220
within the elderly.

211
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:12,880
Osteosarcoma classically arises

212
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:14,520
in the metaphysis of long bones.

213
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:16,620
Again, here's a picture of bone.

214
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,580
You've got a growth plate here.

215
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:20,720
And so what's above the growth plate

216
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,760
is called the epiphysis.

217
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:23,560
The region of the growth plate

218
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,640
is called the metaphysis.

219
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:26,260
And this long shaft here

220
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:27,300
is called the diaphysis.

221
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,120
So osteosarcoma

222
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,220
normally occurs

223
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,220
in the metaphysis.

224
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:33,040
And that's particularly high yield

225
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:33,900
for board exams.

226
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,860
Now, it'll usually occur

227
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:36,600
in the long bone.

228
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,020
Classically, the distal femur

229
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:40,280
or the proximal tibia,

230
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:42,240
so around the region of the knee.

231
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:43,980
It can present

232
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,220
as pathologic fracture,

233
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,180
which basically means

234
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:48,480
that the tumor weakens the bone.

235
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:49,880
which then makes the bone

236
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,820
susceptible to fracture,

237
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,360
i.e. the fracture occurs

238
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,180
because there's some sort of pathology

239
00:07:55,180 --> 00:07:56,640
underlying in the bone.

240
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,020
Or it can present

241
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,740
with bone pain with swelling.

242
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,020
In either case,

243
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,220
an x-ray would be performed.

244
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,100
And this is the classic finding

245
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:05,420
that would be seen on x-ray.

246
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,600
Here you can see

247
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,120
that there's a destructive lesion

248
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,200
growing within the bone.

249
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:11,280
This represents osteosarcoma.

250
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:12,860
And one of the high yield things

251
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:14,460
that examiners like to know

252
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,800
is that osteosarcoma,

253
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,020
as it begins to grow

254
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:18,060
and expand the bone

255
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:19,100
and eventually go into

256
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,400
the adjacent soft tissue,

257
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:21,780
one of the things

258
00:08:21,780 --> 00:08:22,500
that it will do

259
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:23,660
is that it will drag

260
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:24,740
the periosteum,

261
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,660
which is a layer

262
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:26,460
of connective tissue

263
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,460
attached to the bone,

264
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:28,560
off the bone.

265
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:30,180
So imagine here,

266
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:31,620
if this is the surface of bone

267
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:32,100
and it's covered

268
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:33,020
with periosteum,

269
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,100
you can clearly see

270
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:34,580
that here,

271
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,320
the periosteum

272
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:35,980
is being lifted

273
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,660
off the bone.

274
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:37,680
Now that creates

275
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:39,380
an angle right here

276
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,940
called Codman's angle.

277
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:42,080
And board examiners

278
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:42,780
like you to know

279
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:44,220
that Codman's angle

280
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:45,960
is a sign of osteosarcoma.

281
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:47,020
In addition,

282
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:48,540
with osteosarcoma,

283
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:49,580
sometimes you can see

284
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:52,020
this hazy radio opacity

285
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:53,540
coming from the tumor,

286
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:54,920
which almost looks like

287
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,240
the burst of sunlight

288
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,460
coming off the horizon.

289
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:58,720
It's not very well

290
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,920
illustrated in this image.

291
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,400
It basically represents

292
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,720
the tiny fragments of bone

293
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:03,460
being produced

294
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:05,120
by the osteosarcoma.

295
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,780
If a biopsy was performed,

296
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,160
the key finding would be

297
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:10,380
large pleomorphic cells,

298
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,580
i.e. high-grade malignant cells,

299
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:13,680
that are producing

300
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:15,640
this pink matrix

301
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:16,860
called osteoid.

302
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,840
Again, pleomorphic cells

303
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,440
that are producing osteoid

304
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:21,980
is the hallmark on biopsy.

305
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:23,480
Giant cell tumor

306
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,860
is a tumor comprised

307
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:26,780
of multinucleated giant cells

308
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:27,700
and stromal cells.

309
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,640
It occurs in young adults.

310
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:31,660
One of the very high-yield points

311
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:32,460
is that it arises

312
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:33,340
in the epiphysis.

313
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:34,280
Now, of course,

314
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:35,520
this is the diaphysis,

315
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:37,260
and here is the metaphysis,

316
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:38,820
and up here is the epiphysis.

317
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,500
Now, this is very important

318
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:42,220
because it's the only tumor

319
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,520
that you need to know

320
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,760
that's going to arise

321
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:45,540
in the epiphysis.

322
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:46,980
And so on board exam,

323
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:48,420
if you have an epiphyseal tumor,

324
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:49,380
that's basically

325
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,320
giant cell of bone.

326
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:51,700
It usually arises

327
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:52,700
in the distal femur

328
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,820
or the proximal tibia

329
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:54,620
around the knee,

330
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:55,820
and it's kind of similar

331
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:56,460
in location

332
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:58,120
to osteosarcoma, actually.

333
00:09:58,800 --> 00:09:59,500
Now, on x-ray,

334
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:00,440
you'll see something called

335
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:01,720
the soap bubble appearance,

336
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:02,780
and the idea here

337
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,000
is this is the diaphysis,

338
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,320
and then this is the metaphysis,

339
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:08,080
and up here is the epiphysis.

340
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,760
You get the tumor growing,

341
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:11,380
and in response to the tumor,

342
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:12,120
you get a little bit

343
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,800
of reactive bone formation

344
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,340
circling the tumor,

345
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,640
and a bunch of these

346
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:18,780
little areas of bone

347
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:20,680
reacting against the tumor form,

348
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:21,700
and so it produces

349
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:22,440
these bubbles

350
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,600
that look like soap bubbles

351
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,460
in the epiphysis.

352
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:28,080
So, soap bubbles in the epiphysis

353
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,960
is giant cell tumor of bone.

354
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:32,480
This is a locally aggressive tumor

355
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:33,620
that may recur.

356
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:35,600
Ewing sarcoma

357
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,860
is a malignant proliferation

358
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:39,100
of poorly differentiated cells

359
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,240
derived from neuroectoderm.

360
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:42,620
Board examiners like you to know

361
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:43,940
that Ewing sarcoma

362
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:45,900
is derived from neuroectoderm.

363
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:48,620
It arises in the diaphysis

364
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:49,520
of long bones,

365
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,840
usually in male children,

366
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,900
so basically it would be here,

367
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,020
and it grows inside

368
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:56,220
the medullary cavity.

369
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:57,400
Now, as it grows

370
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,660
inside the medullary cavity,

371
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,780
it is then going to push

372
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:02,600
on the surface of the bone,

373
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:03,680
and as it pushes

374
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:04,880
on the surface of the bone,

375
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,360
you're going to get layering

376
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:09,080
of new bone by the periosteum.

377
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,300
Remember that the periosteum

378
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:11,160
is a connected tissue

379
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:12,260
that surrounds the bone,

380
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:13,760
and it also has the ability

381
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,760
to produce new bone.

382
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,260
In fact, when you get a fracture,

383
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:16,960
for example,

384
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,300
it's the periosteum

385
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:19,400
that forms the new bone.

386
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,360
And so, as you put pressure

387
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,800
on the surface of this bone

388
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:24,120
with the tumor growing in it,

389
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,780
the periosteum will begin

390
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:27,860
to lay down layers of new bone.

391
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:29,540
Now, those layers of new bone

392
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:30,740
will have an onion skin

393
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:31,660
appearance on x-ray.

394
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:32,400
Imagine if you looked

395
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,300
at the bone head-on,

396
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:34,540
you would see sort of

397
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,500
an onion skin layer,

398
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:36,280
another layer,

399
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,040
another layer,

400
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,380
as the periosteum

401
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:39,380
is being laid down,

402
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:40,940
trying to protect the bone

403
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:41,700
from this tumor

404
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:42,740
that's growing inside.

405
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,280
And these cells

406
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:52,580
resemble lymphocytes.

407
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:53,820
And that's very important

408
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,000
because it can be confused

409
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:55,740
with two things.

410
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:56,400
Number one,

411
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:57,280
it could be confused

412
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,180
with lymphoma.

413
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,420
And number two,

414
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:00,240
it can be confused

415
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:01,680
with chronic osteomyelitis.

416
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,040
Now, one of the interesting

417
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,440
things about Ewing sarcoma

418
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,720
is that some patients

419
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:06,760
can present with fever.

420
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,060
Now, imagine if you have

421
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:09,160
a patient that has swelling

422
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:09,700
of the bone

423
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:10,380
and has fever,

424
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,360
one of the things

425
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,000
that you're going to think

426
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,860
about is osteomyelitis.

427
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:14,980
So, it can be confused

428
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:15,620
with number one,

429
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:16,180
lymphoma,

430
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:17,160
or number two,

431
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,140
osteomyelitis.

432
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:20,180
And what I clearly distinguish

433
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:21,860
these cells from both lymphoma

434
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:22,860
and osteomyelitis

435
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:24,540
is the fact that

436
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:25,560
these cells

437
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:28,860
have an 11-22 translocation.

438
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,160
And that 11-22 translocation

439
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,720
is particularly high yield

440
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,060
for Ewing sarcoma.

441
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:36,460
Ewing sarcoma is fairly aggressive

442
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:37,560
and it often presents

443
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:38,360
with metastasis,

444
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:40,100
but it also responds well

445
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:40,840
to chemotherapy.

446
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,880
Moving on to cartilage tumors,

447
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:43,760
let me just highlight

448
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,360
a couple simple principles

449
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:46,500
that will make this discussion

450
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,160
very easy.

451
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:48,340
Number one,

452
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:49,560
cartilage tumors

453
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:50,720
can be benign or malignant.

454
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:52,320
Benign cartilage tumor,

455
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:53,140
chondroma,

456
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,100
a malignant cartilage tumor

457
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,000
is called a chondrosarcoma.

458
00:12:57,460 --> 00:12:58,140
Number two,

459
00:12:58,380 --> 00:12:59,660
cartilage tumors arise

460
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:00,380
in the medulla.

461
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:01,620
So, remember that

462
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:02,540
when you have bone,

463
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:03,400
you have a cortex

464
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,420
and you have a medulla,

465
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,080
cartilage tumors normally

466
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,740
arise in the medulla.

467
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:09,140
Number three,

468
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,480
benign tumors,

469
00:13:10,620 --> 00:13:11,620
i.e. chondroma,

470
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,620
they occur in the small bones

471
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:14,660
of the hands and the feet.

472
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,560
And malignant tumors,

473
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,140
i.e. chondrosarcoma,

474
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,240
occur centrally

475
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,180
in the pelvis

476
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:21,500
or the central skeleton.

477
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,080
And those are the key take-homes.

478
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:24,040
Now let's read together.

479
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:25,440
So, chondroma

480
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:27,120
is a benign tumor of cartilage.

481
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,100
It arises in the medulla.

482
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:29,960
Cartilage tumors

483
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,160
normally arise in the medulla.

484
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:32,580
And because it's benign,

485
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:33,920
it'll be in the small bones

486
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:34,940
in the hands and the feet.

487
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:35,960
Here's a picture

488
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,680
of the tubular

489
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:37,480
or small bones

490
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,100
of the hands.

491
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,400
And you can clearly see

492
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,660
that there's this mass

493
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:42,160
growing in the medullary space.

494
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:42,900
And again,

495
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:44,560
this represents a chondroma.

496
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:46,100
Chondrosarcoma

497
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,080
is a malignant

498
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,320
cartilage-forming tumor.

499
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:49,020
Again,

500
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:50,380
because it's a cartilage tumor,

501
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:51,220
it usually arises

502
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:51,920
in the medulla.

503
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,520
But in this particular case,

504
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,520
it'll be in the medulla

505
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,280
of the pelvis

506
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:56,680
or the central skeleton.

507
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:57,780
And so these are

508
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:58,880
some of the basic high yields

509
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,540
concerning cartilage-forming tumors.

510
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:02,340
The final discussion

511
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:03,700
involves metastatic tumors.

512
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:05,000
Metastatic tumors

513
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:05,760
are more common

514
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,700
than primary tumors

515
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:07,240
in the bone.

516
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:08,900
They usually result

517
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,700
in osteolytic lesions

518
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:11,740
or punched-out lesions

519
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:12,280
of the bone.

520
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,040
However,

521
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:14,680
one important high-yield exception

522
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,820
is prostate cancer.

523
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:17,340
This usually produces

524
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:18,920
an osteoblastic lesion.

525
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:20,240
And so what that means

526
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:20,940
is that when you look

527
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:21,440
at the bone,

528
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:22,380
instead of having this

529
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,920
punched-out circular space,

530
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:24,680
as would occur

531
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:26,020
in osteolytic lesions,

532
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,340
in an osteoblastic lesion,

533
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:29,540
you get activation

534
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:30,640
of the osteoblast,

535
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,300
and they begin

536
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:32,660
to lay down bone

537
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:34,040
adjacent to the tumor,

538
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:35,280
and that gives you

539
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:36,420
sclerosis of the bone.

540
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:37,260
And so again,

541
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,500
prostate carcinoma

542
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:39,680
classically produces

543
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,100
osteoblastic lesions.

544
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,380
And that concludes

545
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:42,980
our discussion

546
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:43,840
of bone tumors.

